   },
   "result": {
    "assets": []
   },
   "is_error": false
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I'm sorry the process felt slow. We needed a verification that worked without your phone, so I went to Helena.\n\n**Lost phone:** I can't see any company-issued phone assigned to you, so it looks like a personal device. I can't take any further action on it from here. If you'd like to talk to a person at the desk, tell me and I'll hand you over.\n\n**Taxi company and carrier:** I don't have company guidance on either. These are the usual steps:\n- **Carrier:** Call them to suspend the line or SIM, so nobody can use your number. You can ask them to block the device as well.\n- **Taxi company:** Report it as lost property. Most companies have a lost-property line or form, and you'll need the trip details from your receipt or app.\n- **Find My iPhone:** If it's an iPhone, use Find My to mark it as lost or remotely wipe it. This is the most important step, because it locks the device down.\n- **Other accounts:** Change the passwords on any personal accounts that were signed in on the phone, such as email and banking.\n\nYour old MFA device is removed, so the lost phone can no longer approve sign-ins to your work account. When you have the new phone, sign in and follow the prompts to register it."
  }
